# Post-3.7.1 main is wrong

**ALL code committed to `main` since the 3.7.1 release is wrong.** Do not treat it as correct, as a bisect endpoint, or as a “known good” smoke baseline.

## Never

- **Never bisect git** (no `git bisect`, no checkout of older SHAs / `main` / other branches to “compare”)
- Never check out `main` (or post-3.7.1 commits on it) to see “if the ROM worked before”
- Never copy or replay diffs that landed on main after 3.7.1 as the fix
- Never move HEAD off the user’s active fix branch for debugging

## Do instead

- Stay on the user’s current branch/worktree
- Read the **issues** that need fixing; implement them **newly** on the fix branch
- Debug with logs, generated codegen, rebuilds, and targeted edits on the current tree only
- If historical comparison is required, ask the user first — separate clone/worktree only with explicit approval
